<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Database>
    <EnglishText>
        <Row Tag="LOC_12016A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Dr. Rizal at the Heian Court</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_12016A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The good doctor Rizal finds kindred spirits among the Heian nobility, discussing poetry with them on a moonlit terrace. Yet as they begin another collaborative composition, he cannot help noticing the stack of unopened petitions.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_12016B_NAME">
            <Text>Ah, but inspiration is a fickle beast.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_12016B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_12016C_NAME">
            <Text>At least open one petition.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_12016C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11124A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>I Sent You My Poetry, Please Respond</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11124A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A noble winces at the awkward metaphors in his future bride's poem. He picks up his brush, knowing she waits for his response behind the rice paper partition.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11124B_NAME">
            <Text>With a proper education, her skill will match her passion.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11124B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Cities.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11124C_NAME">
            <Text>The style is certainly...unique.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11124C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Towns.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11125A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Socially Outranked</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11125A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A commander, flushed with the glow of victory, enters the audience hall. But despite his battlefield skill, his bows are awkward and his garments tattered. From the Heian nobility emerge whispered mockery and barely-stifled chuckles.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11125B_NAME">
            <Text>Teach this provincial some manners.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11125B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11125C_NAME">
            <Text>Show these heroes some compassion.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11125C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11126A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>No Accounting for Taste</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11126A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A young noblewoman of a minor clan is introduced to the Heian court, where taste can make or break reputations. The ladies-in-waiting, teeth lacquered a fashionable black, scrutinize everything from the powder on her face to the composition of her jūnihitoe.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11126B_NAME">
            <Text>How strong you must be, to wear such rough-spun silk?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11126B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in {2_capital}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11126C_NAME">
            <Text>Just out of the rice-field, and already the talk of the capital!</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11126C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in {2_capital}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11127A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Buzzkill</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11127A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Vines cover the stones of buildings left in ruins for years. Frustrated with court complacency, a delegation of displaced villagers approaches the palace gates, demanding to be heard.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11127B_NAME">
            <Text>Permit entry. A ruler's duty is to their subjects.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11127B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Towns.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11127C_NAME">
            <Text>Deny entry. The party is just getting good.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11127C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11128A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Yumi</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11128A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A soldier lowers his bow to watch the final moments of a ship at sea, struck down by a single arrow. The soldier rubs his finger instinctively against the laminated bamboo, ignoring the wind and rain slapping his face.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11128B_NAME">
            <Text>Launch another arrow to make sure.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11128B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Yumi Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11128C_NAME">
            <Text>Show respect to the fallen.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11128C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11129A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Ill Tidings</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11129A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>In the aftermath of the deluge that hit {1_Capital}, government officials wade through flood water to assess the damage. But in the palace, court advisors speak of the typhoon as an omen.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11129B_NAME">
            <Text>Make the appropriate offerings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11129B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11129C_NAME">
            <Text>Aid in the rebuilding.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11129C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11130A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Kitsune</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11130A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A new jinja is built, but workers notice a family of foxes, displaced by the new torii gates. Devotees have set up a shrine to the fox-spirit. Such shrines are known for fortune, but also for secrecy and, perhaps, witchcraft.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11130B_NAME">
            <Text>Foxes can make powerful allies.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11130B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11130C_NAME">
            <Text>Keep the focus on the less suspicious kami.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11130C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11131A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Hoo-do</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11131A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A gold phoenix is lowered onto the shingled roof of Hoo-do, its wings extended. The temple's priests watch in quiet contemplation, musing on its completion and the purpose it will serve.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11131B_NAME">
            <Text>Through such masterworks, the ruling class sustains its power.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11131B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11131C_NAME">
            <Text>It is a reminder that enlightenment comes through rebirth.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11131C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Wonders.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11132A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>It's in the Manual</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11132A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A lord surveys his new garden with exasperation. Here is the tranquil pond broken by the shard of rock, there the looming cypress grove. Very little has changed. He demands an answer from his gardener.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11132B_NAME">
            <Text>I have followed nature's own hand.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11132B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11132C_NAME">
            <Text>I will start anew.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11132C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11133A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Value of Gifts</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11133A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Two rival clans offer their appeals to the court: a well-connected but pampered daughter for a bride, or a group of dislocated farmers now seeking urban life.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11133B_NAME">
            <Text>Choose the daughter – influence is priceless.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11133B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Cities, but {2_reward} in Cities.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11133C_NAME">
            <Text>Choose the farmers – population is priceless.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11133C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward} in Cities.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11206A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Transience</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11206A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A bronze bell is struck, its ring carrying far before dissipating. Birdsong brightens the morning air, and then is no more. Lives are lived, and then they are not.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11206B_NAME">
            <Text>They are not gone, but changed.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11206B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11206C_NAME">
            <Text>So it goes.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11206C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11207A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Murasaki Shikibu</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11207A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Lady Murasaki – this is not her real name – is of minor rank, but her rumored knowledge of poetry has opened the doors of the Heian court. A nobody to courtiers who care only for clan rank, she moves at the fringes of banquets, on the edges of court games, unseen, but seeing each lost love, each regret, each heartache.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11207B_NAME">
            <Text>She could be a master of espionage, given the right motivation.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11207B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11207C_NAME">
            <Text>Let her be.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11207C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Tale of Genji</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Lady Murasaki pauses, seeking the right match to her poetry.[nn]"The rushing brook has frozen still, but under clear heaven…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208B_NAME">
            <Text>"…moonlight and shadow wax and wane."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Murasaki nods, in praise of shadows.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208D_NAME">
            <Text>"…I give to you your heart’s desire."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Murasaki frowns. No, not at all. Too direct.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11208E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Lady Sarashina</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Takasue’s daughter travels with her father from the court to his distant holdings. Each night her brush records what she has seen, who they have met, the sights of the road. She claims that she will write each detail of her life as it progresses: her wonder and adventure, loves and losses, age and solitude.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209B_NAME">
            <Text>Encourage her to focus on details – for public administration.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_GOLD] Gold on Active Traditions.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209C_NAME">
            <Text>Encourage her poetic side – for art’s sake.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture on Active Traditions.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209D_NAME">
            <Text>Encourage her to read Tale of Genji.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11209D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture on all Greatworks.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Sarashina Nikki</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Lady Sarashina pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"Why do you come to visit this abandoned old woman…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210B_NAME">
            <Text>"…hidden by the shadows of a moonless night?"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Lady Sarashina nods approvingly. The visitor who hides their visit brings shame with them.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210D_NAME">
            <Text>"…and what joys do you bring to me?"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Lady Sarashina frowns. No, that won’t do. There is no bite.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11210E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Master of Texts</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Caught in a cluster of carts, Sei Shonagon has missed the reading of the sutras. Exiting her carriage hours late and facing the disapproving stares of the other nobles, she gives her apology… quoting the sutras perfectly as she does. Clearly she did not need to be reminded of them.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211B_NAME">
            <Text>Such knowledge! See what she might do instructing students.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211C_NAME">
            <Text>She should learn respect! Put her in her place.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211D_NAME">
            <Text>Lady Murasaki points out two fatal mistakes in Sei’s quotations.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11211D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture on all Greatworks.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Pillow Book</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Sei pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"Inappropriate things. For a Persian to be poor. For a doctor to fall ill."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212B_NAME">
            <Text>"For a soldier to feel fear."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Sei frowns. No, a fearless soldier is too much a fantasy of generals’ dreams.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212D_NAME">
            <Text>"For a butcher to recite scripture."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Sei smiles. One must know one’s place.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11212E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in {2_capital}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11213A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Izumi Shikibu</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11213A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>That Izumi Shikibu is cold, arrogant, and occasionally cutting with words is not disputed. But neither is her skill. Pages fly from her pen, and broken hearts from her doorstep.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11213B_NAME">
            <Text>How can one face yield such destruction? Get her to slow down.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11213B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11213C_NAME">
            <Text>How can one face yield such destruction? Watch the show.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11213C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Although the Wind</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Izumi pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"Although the wind blows fiercely here…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214B_NAME">
            <Text>"The moonlight shines through the beams of this ruined house."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Izumi writes the passage. Moonlight is cold comfort, but comfort nonetheless.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214D_NAME">
            <Text>"The thought of you burns in my breast."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Izumi cringes. Far, far too forceful.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11214E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11215A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Michitsuna’s Mother</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11215A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Most poets capture the ways that loss and heartbreak, love and wonder capture us through metaphors: a cuckoo’s call, a frozen spring. The poet known only as the mother of Michitsuna is more direct, writing plaintively of her own experience.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11215B_NAME">
            <Text>She should, perhaps, get over herself.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11215B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11215C_NAME">
            <Text>Writers should be able to speak bluntly.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11215C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Hours</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet pauses, seeking the right match to this line.[nn]"The hours that I wait alone, in tears, until the break of dawn…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216B_NAME">
            <Text>"The owl and the wood-beetle are my companions."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet frowns. Where is the bite of loss?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216D_NAME">
            <Text>"Can you possibly know how long that is?"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet smiles, a wry twist more pain than pleasure. Can you know? Can you ever?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11216E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} when another Leader targets you with a Diplomatic Sanction.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11217A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Oshikochi no Mitsune</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11217A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Heian poetry lives on paper: love notes passed under paper screens, pressed into eager palms. Too often, it dies with paper: crumpled and tossed aside, ruined by rain or tears. Oshikochi no Mitsune seeks to immortalize the poetry of his time: compile volumes that can be secured in a library, or paint verses on silk screens.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11217B_NAME">
            <Text>Give him what he needs to get it done.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11217B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Library gets +1 Great Work Slot, but {1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11217C_NAME">
            <Text>Verses fall like the spring blossoms; new ones will take their place.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11217C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_GOLD] Gold on all Great Works.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Months and Years</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Oshikochi pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"In spring, the catalpa bows are pulled and released."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218B_NAME">
            <Text>"I feel months and years pass like arrows."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Yes. And each one stings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and an additional +1 every 5 Turns (scaled by Game Speed) to a max of +5.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218D_NAME">
            <Text>"The marshal’s trumpets shake the new blossoms."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Oshikochi frowns. Who cares about soldiers and generals?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11218E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11219A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Ki no Tomonori</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11219A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Ki no Tomonori is a collector of poems, but also of people. His agents scour the land, listening in courtyards, asking pointed questions at banquets. The land needs poets.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11219B_NAME">
            <Text>A poet wants more poets. Convenient. Get back to accounting.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11219B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11219C_NAME">
            <Text>There will be a list of the greatest poets of the ages. Send aid.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11219C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>In the Peaceful Light</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tomonori pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"In the peaceful light, on a spring day when all minds are troubled…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220B_NAME">
            <Text>"Do the cherry blossoms still fall?"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet nods. Even in the midst of human conflict, blossoms and spring, sun and moon, continue.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Towns.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220D_NAME">
            <Text>"The sake cup provides warmth."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet frowns. Illusion upon illusion.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11220E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11221A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Ki no Tsurayuki</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11221A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Ki no Tsurayuki’s brush is bent, its bristles frayed. His hand shakes at times with annoyance as he scrawls his critique of his rival’s latest so-called poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11221B_NAME">
            <Text>Critique is rarely beautiful. More poems, less complaints.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11221B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11221C_NAME">
            <Text>There are structures to good writing. Have him make them clear.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11221C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Twenty Snowy Mountains</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tsurayuki pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"The old master, between twenty snowy mountains. The only things to move…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222B_NAME">
            <Text>"Are his feet."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet frowns. No, no this draws the mind’s eye to human footfalls, when what attracts one to the landscape is that which is not human.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222D_NAME">
            <Text>"A blackbird’s eye."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The poet smiles. Perfect. The smallness of the motion emphasizes the stillness of the scene.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11222E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Natural Wonders Improvements.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11223A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Mibu no Tadamine</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11223A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Two poets face each other in Tadamine’s poetry contest. As Tadamine reads the first line of poetry, each contestant pauses, considering their answer. The first poet gives a classical reference; the second’s is deliberately inappropriate, almost vulgar.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11223B_NAME">
            <Text>Classic skill. The first poet has it.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11223B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11223C_NAME">
            <Text>Subversion requires knowledge. Give the prize to the second.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11223C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>When the Wind Blows</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tadamine pauses, seeking the right match to this line of poetry.[nn]"The snow-heavy clouds parted by the mountain peaks…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224B_NAME">
            <Text>"Can never match the coldness of your heart."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tadamine writes the line, his hand quivering with emotion.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Mining Towns.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224D_NAME">
            <Text>"Bring new life to the spring."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tadamine begins to write, then crumples the paper into a ball. Too boring.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11224E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11225A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Nakayama Tadachika</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11225A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Nakayama Tadachika’s writing house sits on the mountainside, a calm respite from the business of the capital, and is where he retreats when the demands of administration grow too heavy. There, at the base of the mountain, is a bright spot of color: a messenger, bearing some mundane task. Tadachika hides in the rice-basket.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11225B_NAME">
            <Text>Poetry demands solitude. Let the man be.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11225B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+10 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture for each Promotion on all Commanders, but {1_reward} in {2_capital}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11225C_NAME">
            <Text>Send a very large, very strong messenger to get him.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11225C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Great Mirror</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tadachika pauses, seeking the right match to this line.[nn]"Having encountered a shimmering mirror…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226B_NAME">
            <Text>"I can see the past and the future in the present."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tadachika reflects – all we have is the present. All past and future are here, now. The immensity of the revelation stuns him.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226D_NAME">
            <Text>"I can only see your face."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Tadachika sniffs in disapproval. Save it for Izumi.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226E_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11226E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Uta-Awase</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Now, the crowd of Heian nobles assembles to hear something new. A judge provides the first line, and waits to hear what is selected as the second:[nn]"As you take your leave, the moon emerges from the clouds…"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227B_NAME">
            <Text>"It is bright, like my love."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The crowd groans. Too much. Where is the subtlety?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227C_NAME">
            <Text>"Fish dreams."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227C_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The crowd is stunned. “Fish dreams” makes no sense. One person laughs, then another, and then the room is filled with laughter. A noble, wiping tears from his eyes, nods – “good, good."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227D_NAME">
            <Text>"Forgive me. I did not see."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227D_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The moon is the love between the pair, hidden when together, and only revealed upon the lover’s absence. The crowd is silent in approval.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227E_NAME">
            <Text>"Where once we gazed together, I gaze alone."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227E_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Murmurs of assent. It has the right feeling, but it lacks metaphor.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227F_NAME">
            <Text>"And reveals only dew on grass."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227F_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227F_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The moon, here meaning emotion, is often hidden. The dew, like life, burns off in time. The crowd is silent in approval.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227G_NAME">
            <Text>"Only one of us can escape."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227G_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227G_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The crowd groans. Too much. Where is the subtlety?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227H_NAME">
            <Text>"And I still in shadow."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227H_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227H_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Murmurs of approval. The moon – love – is revealed, but only for the departing traveler. The poet is alone, with a darkened heart. Good.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227I_NAME">
            <Text>"And now, I am very sleepy."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227I_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227I_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The crowd groans. What is that supposed to mean?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227J_NAME">
            <Text>"An unwelcome intruder."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227J_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227J_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Murmurs of approval. The moon has interrupted the lovers.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227K_NAME">
            <Text>"A dream within a dream."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227K_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227K_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Hideyoshi’s poem resonates – love, like life, is a dream within a dream.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227L_NAME">
            <Text>"But the darkness had no need of it, as it already was the universe."</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227L_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227L_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Ada’s poem is not the right meter, not the right theme, but its observation is sound.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227M_NAME">
            <Text>"Oh, drink the nectar that life has to offer and let the bitter dregs in peace repose!"</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227M_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227M_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A little too direct, but the sentiment is approved.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227N_NAME">
            <Text>Alexander lays his sword upon the table with a heavy thunk. "Nighttime is dark." he announces.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227N_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Finish the poem.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227N_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The crowd sweats nervously, and nods approval. Nighttime is indeed dark.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227B_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227B_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227C_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227C_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227D_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227D_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227E_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227E_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227F_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227F_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227G_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227G_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227H_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227H_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227I_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227I_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Nothing.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227J_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227J_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227K_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227K_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227L_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227L_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227M_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227M_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227N_COMPLETE_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11227N_COMPLETE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11278A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Heian Monogatari</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11278A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The Heian court wields words sharper than a tachi. The wrong pattern for the season, an inelegant verse, a drop of food spilled on a junihitoe - these can destroy a career. Dealing with foreigners in the court is therefore difficult; they are always, seemingly, wrong.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11278B_NAME">
            <Text>But did you see the foreign ambassador laugh with his mouth open? Like a crocodile.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11278B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11278C_NAME">
            <Text>Decorum is one game. Politics is another. Each has their rules, and the rules do not transfer.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11278C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11279A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>H-Drama</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11279A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Radios sputter to life across Heian lands at the same time every evening, and families gather on tatami mats as the latest installment of Sarashina’s Diary is read. This week, the prince escapes from captivity and tries to send a letter to his lover, but bandits waylay the messenger, and she believes him dead.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11279B_NAME">
            <Text>This is a breath of new life into an old art form.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11279B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11279C_NAME">
            <Text>But the real literature is written.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_11279C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
    </EnglishText>
